<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Anglo-Maratha War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1803–1805</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> War was fought between the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and the Maratha chiefs Scindia of Gwalior, Bhonsle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a> and later Holkar of Indore. British armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-wellesley-1st-duke-of-wellington">Arthur Wellesley</a> and Gerard Lake won at Assaye, Laswari and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1803. The Marathas lost large territories, including Delhi and the Mughal emperor's custody, and the Company became the leading power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
